{"comments": [{"path": "client/scripts/ui/common/UiLabels.cs", "existing_code": "    public static void Apply(Label label, Font font, int size, Color color)
    {
        label.AddThemeFontOverride("font", font);
        label.AddThemeFontSizeOverride("font_size", size);
        label.AddThemeColorOverride("font_color", color);
    }", "content": "`Apply` has no argument validation. It is a public entry point called directly with arbitrary `Font` values (e.g. `UiLabels.Apply(_title, UiFonts.Cjk, ...)`), and `UiFonts.Tech/TechBold` are `GD.Load<Font>` results that return `null` when the asset path is wrong or the font is not yet available. Passing `null` into `AddThemeFontOverride` silently overrides the theme's default font with a null resource, which degrades to invisible/incorrect text with no error — hard to diagnose. Please either guard here (skip the font override when `font` is null) or fail loudly, and likewise validate `label` for null so a caller mistake surfaces immediately instead of throwing a generic NRE deep in Godot.

Also, `size` is unvalidated: a 0/negative size produces invisible labels through every named variant. Consider asserting `size > 0`.", "category": "bug", "severity": "medium", "suggestion_code": "    public static void Apply(Label label, Font font, int size, Color color)
    {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(label);
        if (font is not null)
        {
            label.AddThemeFontOverride("font", font);
        }
        label.AddThemeFontSizeOverride("font_size", size);
        label.AddThemeColorOverride("font_color", color);
    }"}, {"path": "client/scripts/ui/common/UiLabels.cs", "existing_code": "    public static void Cjk(Label label, int size, Color color) =>
        Apply(label, UiFonts.Cjk, size, color);", "content": "`Cjk` replaces the label's font wholesale with a `SystemFont` whose `FontNames` list relies on fonts installed on the host machine (`Microsoft YaHei`, `PingFang SC`, `Noto Sans CJK SC`, `sans-serif`). On platforms without any of these (minimal Linux/SteamOS images, containers, some macOS/Linux CI runners) there is no fallback and CJK strings render as tofu boxes. Additionally, because the whole font is swapped rather than a fallback chain being added, mixed Latin+CJK strings lose the `SpaceGrotesk` Latin glyphs the rest of the UI uses, so typography is inconsistent. Prefer keeping the Tech font as primary and adding the CJK font to `label.GetThemeFont("font").Fallbacks` (or bundling Noto Sans SC) instead of replacing the font outright.", "category": "maintainability", "severity": "medium"}]}

{"comments": [{"path": "client/scripts/ui/settings/SettingsScreen.Layout.cs", "existing_code": "        var speedSub = AddRowLabel(speedRow, "DROP SPEED", $"{s.FallSpeedMultiplier:F1}x");
