1. The sub-label is bound to `FallSpeedMultiplier` while the user edits `FallSpeedLevel`. If these are not kept in sync (e.g. settings loaded with a level whose multiplier differs, or the multiplier is derived elsewhere), the sub-label and the `Lv NN` stepper will show contradictory values. Please confirm the two fields are always consistent and, if so, consider deriving the label from the same source (`FallSpeedLevel`) to avoid drift.
2. `FallSpeedLevel` is clamped to 1..20, but the EFFECTS tab also uses row Y = 500/656/812 below the footer/divider at 876, and more importantly the row Y constants here are absolute design coordinates while the block is built into `root` (the tab root). If the tab content is ever offset, these hard-coded Y values diverge. Use `CreateRow(root, ...)` consistently (which is done) but consider deriving Y from a row index to keep rows inside CardHeight.", "category": "bug", "severity": "medium"}, {"path": "client/scripts/ui/settings/SettingsScreen.Layout.cs", "existing_code": "        AddSegments(modeRow, ModeNames,
