            () => s.NoteBrightnessPercent, value => s.NoteBrightnessPercent = value);", "content": "Slider writes (`NoteBrightnessPercent`, `FlashIntensityPercent`, volumes) store the raw emitted value directly on the settings object. `SettingsSlider` clamps to its own `Min`/`Max`, but the settings object can be loaded from disk with an out-of-range value and then be re-saved unfiltered by `Commit()`/`_ExitTree()`. This is the main path by which "corrupt saved value persists". Consider clamping in the write lambda (or validating in `GameSettings` on load/apply) so a bad persisted value can never propagate.", "category": "bug", "severity": "medium"}, {"path": "client/scripts/ui/settings/SettingsScreen.Layout.cs", "existing_code": "        reset.Pressed += () =>
