                StopInertia();
                GetViewport().SetInputAsHandled();", "content": "`StopInertia()` sets `_state.Display/Target/Written` to `_scroll.ScrollVertical`, which is correct here, but if a drag is interrupted (see the missing-release issue) inertia is stopped on press and never started again, while `_touchId` remains set. Combine resetting touch state with the release path so press/drag/release always pair up.", "category": "bug", "severity": "medium"}, {"path": "client/scripts/ui/song_select/SongListViewport.cs", "existing_code": "    private float WheelScrollPixels(float factor) =>
        (float)(_scroll.GetVScrollBar().Page / 8.0) * factor;", "content": "When the content fits the viewport, `Page` can be 0 (or the bar is hidden), making `WheelScrollPixels` return 0. `Push(0)` with a positive `tau` still returns false but sets `Animating = true`, leaving the state permanently animating toward an unchanged target until `Step` reaches it — a needless per-frame loop. Guard against zero/negative pixels and/or ensure Page > 0 before pushing; also `Push` should early-out when `pixels == 0`.", "category": "performance", "severity": "medium"}, {"path": "client/scripts/ui/song_select/SongListViewport.cs", "existing_code": "    private void Push(float pixels)
    {
