{"comments": [{"path": "editor/scripts/pages/CreatePageOverlay.Drawing.cs", "existing_code": "        if (!System.IO.File.Exists(path)) { color = UiFonts.Giga; return $"FILE NOT FOUND · {name}"; }", "content": "`System.IO.File.Exists` is called from `_Draw`, i.e. once per rendered frame (Godot redraws continuously while hover/glow tweening, and `QueueRedraw` is fired from several paths). The path comes from user input/file dialog, so it may live on a slow network share or a disconnected drive, where `File.Exists` can block for hundreds of ms — and it stalls the render thread. Validation result should be computed when the path changes (on text-changed / file-picked) and cached in a field that `_Draw` only reads. (Same pattern below in `CoverText`.)", "category": "performance", "severity": "high", "suggestion_code": "// Cache on path change (event handler), not in _Draw:
