    {", "content": "There is no synchronization for concurrent writers targeting the same destination (neither `Write` nor `Create`). Two concurrent saves produce two staging directories and two `PublishOverExisting` runs that interleave backup/move/delete of the same target files. A second writer can observe the first writer's in-flight state (missing backups, partially moved set) and compute `desired`/backup lists from it, and a rollback from one writer can restore stale content over the other's published result. Since this is the persistence boundary for the editor, guard publication with an exclusive lock keyed on the normalized destination (named `Mutex` on Windows / lock file on Unix), or fail fast when a staging/publish lock is already held for that destination.", "category": "bug", "severity": "medium"}, {"path": "shared/Chart/V2/V2PackageWriter.cs", "existing_code": "                    V2DiagnosticException(relative, "/", "truncated RIFF/WAVE chunk");", "content": "`ProbeWaveDuration` accepts any `wFormatTag` in {1, 3} with 16 bytes of fmt data and uses the file's declared `nAvgBytesPerSec` for duration, but (a) it never checks consistency (`nAvgBytesPerSec == nSamplesPerSec * nBlockAlign`) or that `dataBytes % nBlockAlign == 0`, so a tampered/corrupt `byteRate` yields a finite but wrong duration that then passes/fails `ValidateAudioBounds` incorrectly; (b) for `WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE` (0xFFFE, tag 1 inside the extension) it is not handled; and (c) chunk advancement `stream.Position = end + (size & 1)` can land past `stream.Length`, aborting the loop silently instead of reporting the trailing truncation (a padded final chunk is fine, but an unpadded odd final chunk that overflows should be a diagnostic). At minimum cross-check byteRate/blockAlign against the data size and treat a final `end + padding` beyond EOF as truncation.", "category": "bug", "severity": "medium"}, {"path": "shared/Chart/V2/V2PackageWriter.cs", "existing_code": "            if (result is null || !double.IsFinite(result.DurationSeconds) ||
