The stated purpose of this type is a "stable client boundary", but it adds no contract of its own: nulls (`pack`, `diff`, or an out-of-range `mode` enum) are forwarded untouched, so callers get a `NullReferenceException` from deep inside `V2Integration` (e.g. `pack.IsV2`, `diff.ChartId`) with no indication of which argument was wrong. Since the doc comment promises a boundary, either validate here or update the comment to make clear that argument/exception handling is delegated. Consider:
```csharp
public static LoadedChart Load(ChartPack pack, ChartDiff diff, ChartLoadMode mode)
{
    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(pack);
    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(diff);
    return V2Integration.Load(pack, diff, mode);
}
