comments.content:
`GD.Load` on a missing/unimported resource returns `null` and prints an error rather than throwing, so a typo'd slug, a renamed `.png`, or a build that omits the `outcomes` subtree would leave `_wordmark.Texture == null` and the result page would silently show a wordmark-less (invisible) prelude with no fallback. This is exactly the failure mode that is hard to see in a release build. Load defensively and degrade to the plain (no-wordmark) prelude instead of rendering an empty TextureRect:

```csharp
var tex = GD.Load<Texture2D>($"res://assets/results/outcomes/{slug}.png");
if (tex is null) GD.PushWarning($"ResultOutcomePrelude: missing wordmark '{slug}'");
_wordmark.Texture = tex;
```

and treat `tex is null` as `HasWordmark == false` (or at minimum keep `_wordmark.Visible = tex is not null`) so the shader/material path isn't exercised against a null texture. Note also that the texture is loaded anew on every `Present` — see the separate lifetime comment.

