comments.content:
`SnapTime(place.Time)` is not re-clamped to `[0, DurationSeconds]` the way `Place` clamps its own output. If snapping rounds up past `DurationSeconds` (e.g. near the end of the chart with a coarse grid), the hover ghost is built at a time beyond the chart duration. The hold branch below uses `Math.Min` which only bounds the top for tool 3; tools 1/2 can produce a negative or >duration hover time. Clamp defensively before constructing the note.

Suggested fix:
```csharp
var time = Clamp(SnapTime(place.Time), 0, DurationSeconds);
if (_tool == 3) time = Math.Min(time, Math.Max(0, DurationSeconds - MinimumHoldDuration(time)));
```

