comments.content:
Once `_age` reaches `Lifetime`, this node keeps running `_Process` and issuing a full redraw every frame forever (the last frame is fully faded, so it draws nothing visible but still costs CPU/GPU). RecycleExpired() only drains the list on the next render update, but if the bloom is ever recycled outside that path — or a caller forgets `SetProcess(false)` like NotePaletteSpecimen does — it burns redraw time indefinitely. Clamp or stop processing on expiry:

```csharp
public override void _Process(double delta)
{
    _age += delta;
    if (_age >= Lifetime)
    {
        SetProcess(false);
        Visible = false;
    }
    QueueRedraw();
}
```
(mirror in ResetFor/ResetForPool: `SetProcess(true)` / `SetProcess(false)`).

