Related to the invariants between `Document.IsUnpersisted` and `Draft`: `AddChart` never re-syncs the draft, so the draft only stays valid by accident (it holds the same `EditorDocument` instance). If a future code path replaces `Document` (e.g. `Open` leaving `Draft` non-null, or a caller assigning `Document` directly), `Save` will happily call `draft.BuildPackageCreateRequest(...)` which builds the request from `Document.BuildPackSnapshot()` of the *draft's* document, not the session's current `Document`. Please assert identity explicitly so this mismatch surfaces as an early, clear error instead of writing the wrong package:

