The assertion message claims "without duplicating prior selection", but at this point the prior selection is empty (the preceding replacement marquee with hits cleared it, and `CancelMarquee` only resets marquee flags). So the de-duplication against existing `NoteIds` (`_noteIds.Add` on already-selected ids) is never exercised. A regression that clobbers or duplicates the pre-existing selection would pass. Seed a prior selection first, e.g.:

```csharp
state.ToggleNote("a");
state.BeginMarquee(true);
state.UpdateMarquee(3);
state.FinishMarquee(["a", "b"]);
Check(state.MarqueeAdditive && state.NoteIds.Count == 2 && state.NoteIds.Contains("a") && state.NoteIds.Contains("b"),
    "additive marquee merges hits with prior selection without duplication");
```

