comments.content:
The disjunction `Health == healthBefore - 1500 || Health == 0` weakens the assertion: after the preceding `ApplyMine(touched: false)` the engine's health is still `DefaultMaxHealth` (10000) and `MaxHealth` is 10000, so the `Health == 0` branch can never legitimately be hit here. More importantly, if the damage formula regresses (e.g. to -1000), and health were already <= 1000 the test would still pass via the `== 0` branch, masking the bug. Derive the expectation from `engine.HealthDelta(ScoreCategory.Mine, JudgeGrade.Miss)` and assert the exact clamped value instead:

```csharp
var expected = Math.Clamp(healthBefore + engine.HealthDelta(ScoreCategory.Mine, JudgeGrade.Miss), 0, engine.MaxHealth);
Check(engine.Health == expected, $"...");
```
Also note `scaled` is never exercised for Mine at the MaxHealth cut-off, so the clamp path is untested.

